research/advanced-qft-supersymmetry-build-2026-10-23-owner-resolution/adhm-before/research/advanced-qft-supersymmetry-build-2026-10-23-batch-12.notes.md-34-The actual batch-5 carrier items/def-qftx-instanton-number-and-asd-sector.md and its complete definition/proof were inspected. Its relevant interface fixes q_B=(8π²)⁻¹∫B(F∧F), B=-tr in the defining SU(2) convention, and the Hodge/self-duality sign. I use only the supplied trace/Hodge conventions and do not extend its SU(2)-only integrality clause to general U(N). Current loadStep1Record plus step1Decision now reports this supplier's current record as ready, with its full listed transitive closure bound into the record. The assigned definition consequently has its required charge interface available; its separate ADHM quotient descriptions remain definitions and do not assert unproved correspondences.
research/advanced-qft-supersymmetry-build-2026-10-23-owner-resolution/adhm-before/research/advanced-qft-supersymmetry-build-2026-10-23-batch-12.notes.md-35-
research/advanced-qft-supersymmetry-build-2026-10-23-owner-resolution/adhm-before/research/advanced-qft-supersymmetry-build-2026-10-23-batch-12.notes.md-36-The current batch-9 carrier items/thm-atiyah-bott-berline-vergne-integration-formula.md was inspected with its actual statement, proof, and direct suppliers. Its Statement is for compact oriented smooth T-manifolds. Its proof cites thm-borel-localization-for-compact-torus-actions, and a current batch-8 carrier is now present. I read its complete statement and proof and compared the interface: it assumes a compact, finite-dimensional, Hausdorff, second-countable smooth T-manifold without boundary and real or rational Borel cohomology using a product Milnor model; the ABBV use is compact real Borel, so the statement supplies the planned compact interface. It makes no noncompact or compact-support assertion. However, the Borel item itself has no current Step-1 readiness record, its Fact [F2] expressly leaves the real character-localization interface conditional because def-qftx-character-localization has no current record, and its direct in-run prerequisite records are absent. ABBV and all four of its direct in-run prerequisite items likewise lack current Step-1 records. These are actual missing readiness inputs, not draft-status or independent-approval objections. I therefore retain the ABBV use as conditional and do not apply compact ABBV directly to the resolved noncompact ADHM quotient.
