research/advanced-qft-supersymmetry-build-2026-10-23-owner-resolution/borel-index-reconciliation/before/research/advanced-qft-supersymmetry-build-2026-10-23-batch-12.pages.json-155-        },
research/advanced-qft-supersymmetry-build-2026-10-23-owner-resolution/borel-index-reconciliation/before/research/advanced-qft-supersymmetry-build-2026-10-23-batch-12.pages.json-156-        "statement": "Let $\\mathfrak M^\\zeta_{1,2}$ be the quotient of $V=\\mathbb C$, $W=\\mathbb C^2$ data $(B_1,B_2,I,J)$ satisfying $[B_1,B_2]+IJ=0$ and $\\operatorname{span}\\{B_1^{m_1}B_2^{m_2}I(W):m_1,m_2\\geq0\\}=V$, modulo $GL(V)$, in the positive stability chamber. Let $t_1,t_2$ be the rotation characters, let $e_1,e_2$ be the dual framing characters, and put $\\epsilon_i=c_1^T(t_i)$ and $a_\\alpha=c_1^T(e_\\alpha)$. The two fixed points are $(\\{(0,0)\\},\\varnothing)$ and $(\\varnothing,\\{(0,0)\\})$. Their tangent characters are respectively\n$$t_1+t_2+\\frac{e_2}{e_1}+t_1t_2\\frac{e_1}{e_2}\\qquad\\text{and}\\qquad t_1+t_2+\\frac{e_1}{e_2}+t_1t_2\\frac{e_2}{e_1}.$$\nTheir Euler classes are\n$$E_1=\\epsilon_1\\epsilon_2(a_2-a_1)(\\epsilon_1+\\epsilon_2+a_1-a_2),\\qquad E_2=\\epsilon_1\\epsilon_2(a_1-a_2)(\\epsilon_1+\\epsilon_2+a_2-a_1).$$\nThus the degree-one coefficient of the fixed-point series is $E_1^{-1}+E_2^{-1}$.\n\nThe diagram records the two partition tuples; each square is one one-dimensional weight space of $V$, and the subscript identifies the framing color.\n\n~~~tikz\n\\begin{tikzpicture}[x=0.75cm,y=0.75cm]\n  \\draw[fill=blue!15] (0,0) rectangle (1,1);\n  \\draw (0,0) grid (1,1);\n  \\node[below] at (0.5,0) {$Y_1$};\n  \\node[below] at (2,0) {$Y_2=\\varnothing$};\n  \\draw[fill=orange!20] (4,0) rectangle (5,1);\n  \\draw (4,0) grid (5,1);\n  \\node[below] at (4.5,0) {$Y_2$};\n  \\node[below] at (6,0) {$Y_1=\\varnothing$};\n\\end{tikzpicture}\n~~~",
