research/advanced-qft-supersymmetry-build-2026-10-23-owner-resolution/adhm-before/items/ex-adhm-u2-one-instanton-fixed-points.md-65-1.1 A two-tuple of partitions with total size one places its single box in exactly one of the two colors, so the only possibilities are $(\{(0,0)\},\varnothing)$ and $(\varnothing,\{(0,0)\})$. Their quotient representatives have $V$-characters $e_1$ and $e_2$, respectively. [given, F2, algebra]
research/advanced-qft-supersymmetry-build-2026-10-23-owner-resolution/adhm-before/items/ex-adhm-u2-one-instanton-fixed-points.md-66-
research/advanced-qft-supersymmetry-build-2026-10-23-owner-resolution/adhm-before/items/ex-adhm-u2-one-instanton-fixed-points.md-67-2.1 For the first point, the ADHM convention [F1] gives $\mathbf W=e_1^{-1}+e_2^{-1}$ and $\mathbf W^\vee=e_1+e_2$, while $\mathbf V=e_1$. Substitution in [F2] gives $$t_1+t_2+\frac{e_2}{e_1}+t_1t_2\frac{e_1}{e_2}.$$ The corresponding additive weights are $\epsilon_1,\epsilon_2,a_2-a_1,\epsilon_1+\epsilon_2+a_1-a_2$, so their product is $E_1$. Interchanging the two colors gives the second displayed character and $E_2$. [given, F1, F2, step 1.1, algebra]
research/advanced-qft-supersymmetry-build-2026-10-23-owner-resolution/adhm-before/items/ex-adhm-u2-one-instanton-fixed-points.md-68-
research/advanced-qft-supersymmetry-build-2026-10-23-owner-resolution/adhm-before/items/ex-adhm-u2-one-instanton-fixed-points.md-69-3.1 Each fixed-point contribution is the reciprocal of its Euler product, so the degree-one coefficient is $E_1^{-1}+E_2^{-1}$. The TikZ drawing only records the two one-box colorings and is not used in this calculation. [given, F2, step 2.1, algebra] ∎
--
