research/advanced-qft-supersymmetry-build-2026-10-23-owner-resolution/adhm-before/items/ex-adhm-u1-one-box-fixed-point.md-30-
research/advanced-qft-supersymmetry-build-2026-10-23-owner-resolution/adhm-before/items/ex-adhm-u1-one-box-fixed-point.md-31-Let $\mathfrak M^\zeta_{1,1}$ be the quotient of $V=W=\mathbb C$ data $(B_1,B_2,I,J)$ satisfying $[B_1,B_2]+IJ=0$ and $\operatorname{span}\{B_1^{m_1}B_2^{m_2}I(W):m_1,m_2\geq0\}=V$, modulo $GL(V)$, in the positive stability chamber. Let $t_1,t_2$ be the two rotation characters and set $\epsilon_i=c_1^T(t_i)$. The datum $B_1=B_2=J=0$, $I=1$ is stable and satisfies the complex moment-map equation. The unique fixed point is the one-box partition $Y_1=\{(0,0)\}$; its tangent character is $t_1+t_2$, its equivariant Euler class is $\epsilon_1\epsilon_2$, and its contribution to the degree-one coefficient of the fixed-point series is $(\epsilon_1\epsilon_2)^{-1}$.
