## Definition

Fix a positive integer "'$N$, an integer $k'"\\geq0"'$, and a real parameter $'"\\zeta>0"'$. Let $V='"\\mathbb C"'^k$ and $W='"\\mathbb C"'^N$ with fixed Hermitian structures. The positive-FI stable ADHM quotient $X_{k,N}''^'"\\zeta"'$ is the geometric quotient by $GL(V)$ of quadruples $(B_1,B_2,I,J)$ with $B_i'"\\in\\operatorname{End}_{\\mathbb C}(V)"'$, $I:W'"\\to V"'$, and $J:V'"\\to W"'$, satisfying $[B_1,B_2]+IJ=0$ and the condition that the vectors $B_{i_1}'"\\cdots B_{i_m}I(w)"'$ span $V$ for all words of length $m'"\\geq0"'$ and $w'"\\in W"'$. This is the positive stability chamber of the complex ADHM quotient; it is not, by definition, the zero-FI regular quotient or the moduli space of anti-self-dual connections.

Let $T_{'"\\mathbb C}=(\\mathbb C"'^'"\\times)"'^2'"\\times(\\mathbb C"'^'"\\times)"'^N$ act algebraically, and let $K=(S''^1)''^2'"\\times(S"'^1)''^N$ be its maximal compact subgroup. The compact action on the ADHM data is $(t_1,t_2,h)'"\\cdot(B_1,B_2,I,J)=(t_1B_1,t_2B_2,Ih"'^{-1},t_1t_2hJ)$, where $h$ acts on $W$ with weights $e_'"\\alpha"'^{-1}$; the same formula with nonzero complex parameters defines the algebraic action. Thus $W$ has character $'"\\mathbf W=\\sum_{\\alpha=1}"'^N e_'"\\alpha"'^{-1}$ and $W''^'"\\vee"'$ has character $'"\\mathbf W"'^'"\\vee=\\sum_{\\alpha=1}"'^N e_'"\\alpha"'$. Write $'"\\epsilon_i=c_1"'^K(t_i)$ and $a_'"\\alpha=c_1"'^K(e_'"\\alpha)"'$; they are degree-two equivariant weights. A fixed-radius S4 application has $'"\\epsilon_i=r"'^{-1}$ and dimensionless variables $r'"\\epsilon_i"'$ and $ra_'"\\alpha"'$. Let $q$ be a dimensionless formal instanton-counting parameter.

For an adjoint hypermultiplet, extend the torus by a flavor circle $U(1)_m$ that acts trivially on the base $X_{k,N}''^'"\\zeta"'$. Let $'"\\mu"'$ be the degree-two equivariant weight of its defining character, let $L_{-1}$ be the associated line of inverse flavor weight, and let $T_m=T_{'"\\mathbb C}\\times\\mathbb C_m"'^'"\\times"'$ with maximal compact subgroup $K_m=K'"\\times S"'^1_m$. For a smooth $X_{k,N}''^'"\\zeta"'$ of complex dimension $2kN$, define the adjoint-mass insertion by the top Chern class
$$'"\\mathcal E_{\\widetilde m}=e_{T_m}(TX_{k,N}"'^'"\\zeta\\otimes L_{-1})\\in H_{T_m}"'^{4kN}(X_{k,N}''^'"\\zeta;\\mathbb Q),"'$$
where the formal parameter $'"\\widetilde m"'$ is the specialization of $'"\\mu"'$. If the tangent weights at a fixed point are $w_1,'"\\ldots,w_{2kN}"'$, the restriction of this insertion is $'"\\prod_j(w_j-\\widetilde m)"'$. In the source'"'s Euclidean mass convention, "'$m=i m_E$ for real hypermultiplet mass $m_E$, and the Ω-equivariant mass is $'"\\widetilde m=m+(\\epsilon_1+\\epsilon_2)/2"'$.

Use the normalized equivariant Borel–Moore groups $H''^{'"\\mathrm{BM},K_m}_j(X;\\mathbb Q)"'$, whose dualizing object restricts to the ordinary dualizing object without a quotient-stack dimension shift. Let $S_{T_m}$ be generated by the first Chern classes of nontrivial integral characters of $T_m$. For each $k$, suppose $X_{k,N}''^'"\\zeta"'$ is smooth of complex dimension $2kN$, has a finite $T_m$-invariant affine atlas, and has a proper fixed locus $F_{k,N}$. When the character-localized proper pushforward $p_{k,*}''^{'"\\mathrm{loc}}=p_{F,*}\\circ(i_*)"'^{-1}$ is defined by the fixed-locus concentration isomorphism and proper trace, set
$$I_{k,N}''^{'"\\mathrm{adj}}(\\widetilde m)=p_{k,*}"'^{'"\\mathrm{loc}}\\bigl(\\mathcal E_{\\widetilde m}\\cap[X_{k,N}"'^'"\\zeta]_{K_m}\\bigr)\\in S_{T_m}"'^{-1}R_{T_m}'"\\subset\\mathbb Q(\\epsilon_1,\\epsilon_2,a_1,\\ldots,a_N,\\widetilde m)."'$$
This is the mass-inserted localized pushforward convention of the named supplier; it is not an ordinary pushforward along a nonproper map. The concentration isomorphism is not asserted to exist here.

Whenever the preceding data are supplied for every $k'"\\geq0"'$, define the formal adjoint-hypermultiplet instanton series by
$$Z_{N,'"\\mathrm{adj}}"'^{'"\\mathrm{loc}}(q;\\widetilde m)=\\sum_{k\\geq0}q"'^k I_{k,N}''^{'"\\mathrm{adj}}(\\widetilde m)."'$$
The series is coefficientwise formal and has no asserted analytic convergence. The current S4 postulate selects the $N=2$ case with one adjoint hypermultiplet; its physical mass, coupling, radius, continued Coulomb contour, and noncommutative regulator are supplied by that model input.

