## Example

Take $N=2$ and charge $k=1$ in the formal ADHM series, and assume the localized pushforward and model conditions of the fixed-point theorem. Exactly one box can lie in either color, so the fixed-point tuples are $(\square,\varnothing)$ and $(\varnothing,\square)$. Put $s=\epsilon_1+\epsilon_2$ and $d=a_2-a_1$. Their tangent characters and Euler classes are
$$
\begin{aligned}
\operatorname{ch}_T(T_{(\square,\varnothing)}X)&=t_1+t_2+\frac{e_2}{e_1}+t_1t_2\frac{e_1}{e_2},&E_1&=\epsilon_1\epsilon_2d(s-d),\\
\operatorname{ch}_T(T_{(\varnothing,\square)}X)&=t_1+t_2+\frac{e_1}{e_2}+t_1t_2\frac{e_2}{e_1},&E_2&=-\epsilon_1\epsilon_2d(s+d).
\end{aligned}
$$
For generic weights with $d(s-d)(s+d)\ne0$, the coefficient of $q$ is
$$E_1^{-1}+E_2^{-1}=\frac{1}{\epsilon_1\epsilon_2d(s-d)}-\frac{1}{\epsilon_1\epsilon_2d(s+d)}=\frac{2}{\epsilon_1\epsilon_2(s^2-d^2)}.$$
