## Statement

Fix $N\geq1$, $k\geq0$, and $\zeta>0$. Use the positive-FI stable complex ADHM quotient $X_{k,N}^\zeta$ of the preceding definition, with $T=(S^1)^2\times(S^1)^N$ acting by $(t_1,t_2,h)\cdot(B_1,B_2,I,J)=(t_1B_1,t_2B_2,Ih^{-1},t_1t_2hJ)$ and framing character $\mathbf W=\sum_{\alpha=1}^N e_\alpha^{-1}$. Write $K_N=\mathbb Q(\epsilon_1,\epsilon_2,a_1,\ldots,a_N)$, where $\epsilon_i=c_1^T(t_i)$ and $a_\alpha=c_1^T(e_\alpha)$ are algebraically independent, and let $q$ be the dimensionless formal charge-counting variable. For an $N$-tuple of partitions $\vec Y=(Y_1,\ldots,Y_N)$, each $Y_\alpha$ a finite downward-closed subset of $\mathbb Z_{\geq0}^2$, put $|\vec Y|=\sum_\alpha|Y_\alpha|$, $\mathbf V_{\vec Y}=\sum_{\alpha=1}^N e_\alpha\sum_{(i,j)\in Y_\alpha}t_1^it_2^j$, and $\mathbf W^\vee=\sum_\alpha e_\alpha$. Assume the complexification of $T$ acts algebraically on a smooth separated finite-type complex structure on $X_{k,N}^\zeta$, with a finite invariant affine atlas and finite proper fixed locus. Assume the fixed points and tangent characters are the partition-indexed data stated below, and that the localized equivariant Borel–Moore pushforward from the complex-oriented fundamental class is defined by the proper-fixed-locus construction and obeys its noncompact localization formula. Finally, assume the adopted four-dimensional $\mathcal N=2$ S4 model selects compact gauge group $U(N)$ and a local pole regulator whose formal instanton factor is the localized series in the preceding definition.

Then for each $k$ the fixed locus is finite and is indexed by the $N$-tuples $\vec Y$ of total size $k$. Its tangent character is
$$\operatorname{ch}_T(T_{\vec Y}X_{k,N}^\zeta)=\mathbf V_{\vec Y}^{\vee}\mathbf V_{\vec Y}(t_1+t_2-1-t_1t_2)+\mathbf V_{\vec Y}^{\vee}\mathbf W^\vee+t_1t_2\mathbf W\mathbf V_{\vec Y}.$$
For each tangent character $\chi$, let $u_\chi=c_1^T(\chi)$, and let $E_{\vec Y}$ be the product of these additive weights with multiplicity. The localized pushforward coefficient and the resulting formal series are
$$I_{k,N}=\sum_{|\vec Y|=k}E_{\vec Y}^{-1},\qquad Z_N^{\mathrm{loc}}(q)=\sum_{k\geq0}q^k\sum_{|\vec Y|=k}E_{\vec Y}^{-1}\in K_N[[q]].$$

For an S4 application of radius $R$, the source-specific convention specializes the dimensionless rotation weights to $R\omega_1=R\omega_2=1$ and evaluates the local factor at its stated Coulomb contour and coupling. The equality above remains an identity of formal rational functions at generic parameters; a contour prescription is needed at poles. This theorem does not assert existence of the four-dimensional path integral, equality with the full S4 partition function, removal of the noncommutative/FI regulator, or convergence of the formal series.

