        "statement": "Fix a positive integer $N$, an integer $k\\geq0$, and a real parameter $\\zeta>0$. Let $V=\\mathbb C^k$ and $W=\\mathbb C^N$ with fixed Hermitian structures. The positive-FI stable ADHM quotient $X_{k,N}^\\zeta$ is the geometric quotient by $GL(V)$ of quadruples $(B_1,B_2,I,J)$ with $B_i\\in\\operatorname{End}_{\\mathbb C}(V)$, $I:W\\to V$, and $J:V\\to W$, satisfying $[B_1,B_2]+IJ=0$ and the condition that the vectors $B_{i_1}\\cdots B_{i_m}I(w)$ span $V$ for all words of length $m\\geq0$ and $w\\in W$. This is the positive stability chamber of the complex ADHM quotient; it is not, by definition, the zero-FI regular quotient or the moduli space of anti-self-dual connections.\n\nLet $T_{\\mathbb C}=(\\mathbb C^\\times)^2\\times(\\mathbb C^\\times)^N$ act algebraically, and let $K=(S^1)^2\\times(S^1)^N$ be its maximal compact subgroup. The compact action on the ADHM data is $(t_1,t_2,h)\\cdot(B_1,B_2,I,J)=(t_1B_1,t_2B_2,Ih^{-1},t_1t_2hJ)$, where $h$ acts on $W$ with weights $e_\\alpha^{-1}$; the same formula with nonzero complex parameters defines the algebraic action. Thus $W$ has character $\\mathbf W=\\sum_{\\alpha=1}^N e_\\alpha^{-1}$ and $W^\\vee$ has character $\\mathbf W^\\vee=\\sum_{\\alpha=1}^N e_\\alpha$. For a character $\\chi$ write $u_\\chi=c_1^K(\\chi|_K)$, and let $S_T$ be the multiplicative set generated by $u_\\chi$ for nontrivial integral characters. The coefficient ring is $R_T=H^*(BK;\\mathbb Q)=\\mathbb Q[\\epsilon_1,\\epsilon_2,a_1,\\ldots,a_N]$, with all generators in degree two, and $K_N=\\operatorname{Frac}(R_T)$. The localization $S_T^{-1}R_T$ embeds canonically in $K_N$. In a fixed-radius $R$ application with $\\hbar=c=1$, the dimensionless variables are $R\\epsilon_i$ and $Ra_\\alpha$; the formal counting variable $q$ is dimensionless and is not identified with a physical coupling by this definition.\n\nUse the normalized equivariant Borel–Moore groups $H^{\\mathrm{BM},K}_j(X;\\mathbb Q)$, whose dualizing object restricts to the ordinary dualizing object without a quotient-stack dimension shift. For each $k$, suppose $X_{k,N}^\\zeta$ has a smooth complex structure of dimension $2kN$, a finite $T_{\\mathbb C}$-invariant affine atlas, and a proper fixed locus $F_{k,N}=(X_{k,N}^\\zeta)^{T_{\\mathbb C}}$. Let $i:F_{k,N}\\hookrightarrow X_{k,N}^\\zeta$ be inclusion. When the character-localized Borel–Moore concentration map $i_*:S_T^{-1}H_*^{\\mathrm{BM},K}(F_{k,N};\\mathbb Q)\\to S_T^{-1}H_*^{\\mathrm{BM},K}(X_{k,N}^\\zeta;\\mathbb Q)$ is an isomorphism, define the intrinsic localized pushforward by $p_{k,*}^{\\mathrm{loc}}=p_{F,*}\\circ(i_*)^{-1}$, where $p_F:F_{k,N}\\to\\mathrm{pt}$ is proper. The complex orientation gives the equivariant Borel–Moore fundamental class $[X_{k,N}^\\zeta]_K$, and set $I_{k,N}=p_{k,*}^{\\mathrm{loc}}([X_{k,N}^\\zeta]_K)\\in S_T^{-1}R_T\\subset K_N$. This is the normalized localized pushforward convention of the named supplier; it is not an ordinary pushforward along the nonproper map $X_{k,N}^\\zeta\\to\\mathrm{pt}$. The required concentration isomorphism is not asserted here.\n\nWhenever these data are specified for every $k\\geq0$, the regulated ADHM equivariant instanton series is the formal series $Z_N^{\\mathrm{loc}}(q)=\\sum_{k\\geq0}q^k I_{k,N}\\in K_N[[q]]$. The series is defined coefficientwise and has no asserted analytic convergence. Its use as a factor in a particular four-dimensional field-theory partition function requires a separate adopted model and regulator input."
