[A1] Assume the source-reported N=2* instanton factor uses the mass-inserted tangent Euler class $'"\\prod_\\chi(w_\\chi-\\widetilde m)"'$ over the vector tangent Euler class. The source'"'s §5 equation (5.11) gives this shifted-weight numerator and "'$'"\\widetilde m=m+(\\epsilon_1+\\epsilon_2)/2"'$; this is a formal regulator convention, not a proof of a continuum determinant or path-integral equality.

[A2] Assume the fixed-point, tangent-character, smoothness, finite-atlas, and proper-fixed-locus claims of [F2] apply under its exact positive-FI hypotheses. This proof uses only that stable quotient result; it makes no ADHM-to-ASD or ADHM-to-Gieseker identification and takes the separate pushforward from [F4].

[A3] Assume the localized Borel–Moore construction [F3] and formula [F4] are available for this quotient and for the flavor-extended torus, with the smooth finite-type action, finite invariant affine atlas, and proper finite fixed locus required by [F4]. The current records for the batch-61 carriers are missing, so this remains conditional.

[A4] Assume the exact source regulator input [L1] identifies the formal local factor of the adopted N=2* U(2) S4 model with the mass-inserted series for $N=2$ under the stated Euclidean mass shift. The current postulate carrier exists but lacks its batch-50 Step 1 readiness record; no full S4 integral or regulator construction is inferred.

## Proof

1.1 By [A2] and [F2], the $T$-fixed points of $X_{k,N}''^'"\\zeta"'$ are isolated and correspond bijectively to the $N$-tuples $'"\\vec Y"'$ with $|'"\\vec Y|=k"'$. The tangent character at each point is the displayed character, so its additive weights, with multiplicity, have Euler product $E_{'"\\vec Y}"'$. [given, A2, F2]

2.1 Extend $T$ by the flavor circle acting trivially on the base. This does not change the fixed-point set, and at $'"\\vec Y"'$ the top Chern insertion restricts to $N_{'"\\vec Y}(\\widetilde m)=\\prod_\\chi(w_\\chi-\\widetilde m)"'$ by the definition in [F1]. Since all tangent characters are nontrivial, their Chern classes are inverted in the localized coefficient field. [given, F1, F2, step 1.1, algebra]

2.2 Apply the noncompact Borel–Moore localization formula [F4] under [A3] to $'"\\mathcal E_{\\widetilde m}\\cap[X_{k,N}"'^'"\\zeta]"'$. Each fixed component is a proper point, its proper trace is evaluation, and its normal bundle is the tangent representation; hence the coefficient is the finite sum $'"\\sum_{|\\vec Y|=k}N_{\\vec Y}(\\widetilde m)/E_{\\vec Y}"'$. Its Borel–Moore degree is zero because $c_{2kN}$ has degree $4kN$, equal to the degree of the fundamental class. [F1, F3, F4, A3, step 1.1, step 2.1]

3.1 By the definition [F1], the pushforward in step 2.2 is $I_{k,N}''^{'"\\mathrm{adj}}(\\widetilde m)"'$. For finite $N$ and fixed $k$ there are finitely many partition tuples, so each coefficient is a finite rational function in the stated field. The coefficient sequence therefore defines the displayed formal power series; at $k=0$, the unique empty tuple has empty numerator and denominator products equal to $1$. [F1, F2, step 2.2, algebra]

4.1 Under the source-reported insertion convention [A1] and the exact model input [A4], the $N=2$ specialization of step 3.1 is the formal local N=2* instanton factor with $'"\\epsilon_1=\\epsilon_2=r"'^{-1}$, $'"\\widetilde m=i m_E+r"'^{-1}$, and the model'"'s "'$q$ and continued Coulomb contour. The argument proves only this conditional fixed-point formula; it establishes neither the assumed S4 regulator nor a continuum functional integral. [given, A1, A4, L1, step 3.1] ∎
